# packsquash rules

## Philosophy

- Smallest diff wins. Three similar lines beat premature helper. (But when updating keep everything consistent with each other)
- Less code with same behavior always wins. Equivalent solutions: shorter one ships. Compression is intelligence, but not an excuse on lazyness or forgetting.
- Don't over-guard. Check only conditions that can actually occur. Dead defensive code isn't safety.
- No comments unless asked. Keep existing ones, they carry context.
- Delete dead code. Don't comment out.
- Natural human text in errors, descriptions, toasts. No dashes, no robotic phrasing. Descriptions start capitalized, end with period.
- One patch per concern. But when updating keep everything consistent with each other.
